  "solution": "The logic followed here is : (Cube of 1st number) + (Cube of 2nd number) = 3rd number\n\nGiven :\n\n \n• \n \n(3, 2, 35) \n\n \n\n(3)³ + (2)³ = 35\n\n27 + 8 = 35\n\n35 = 35 (LHS = RHS)\n\n \n• \n \n(1, 4, 65)​\n\n \n\n(1)³ + (4)³ = 65\n\n1 + 64 = 65\n\n65 = 65 (LHS = RHS)\n\n​So,\n\n \n• Option - (1) : (7, 2, 351)​\n\n(7)³ + (2)³ = 351\n\n343 + 8 = 351\n\n**351 = 351 (LHS = RHS)**\n\n \n• Option - (2) : (3, 2, 31)​\n\n(3)³ + (2)³ = 31\n\n27 + 8 = 31\n\n**35 ≠ 31 (LHS ≠ RHS)**\n\n \n• Option - (3) : (5, 4, 41)​\n\n(5)³ + (4)³ = 41\n\n125 + 64 = 41\n\n**189 ≠ 41 (LHS ≠ RHS)**\n\n \n• Option - (4) : (6, 8, 224)​​\n\n(6)³ + (8)³ = 224\n\n216 + 512 = 224\n\n**728 ≠ 224 (LHS ≠ RHS)**\n\n​Hence,** \"Option - (1)\"** is the correct answer.\n\n91:T141d,\n<",
